    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4ki5u4t",
      "content": "Diseases are abnormal conditions that negatively affect the structure or function of an organism. They may be caused by pathogens, nutritional deficiency, genetic factors or lifestyle habits."
    },
    {
      "id": "chptmq8",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Communicable vs Non-Communicable Diseases"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ezhhe8v",
      "content": "Communicable diseases spread from one person to another through air, water, contact or vectors. Non-communicable diseases do not spread and are often related to lifestyle, genetics or deficiency."
    },
